# Line endings are decided here, not by each machine's git config.
#
# Windows checks out with core.autocrlf=true by default, so every source file
# arrives with CRLF -- and spotless (palantir-java-format, endWithNewline) then
# fails the build on files nobody edited. Running CI on Windows without this
# reports a formatting violation on all 218 files and says nothing at all about
# the change being tested.
#
# Normalised in the repository, LF in every working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe is the exception: a .cmd whose last line lacks CRLF can execute without
# the terminator it expects. The Windows launcher in every release archive is one
# of these.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.onnx binary
*.jar binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
